& [ResolutionInterface] is a library construction seam capable of receiving a retrieval request
& [ResolutionCapability] is an admitted implementation that can obtain material beyond the current in-memory document
  + interface presence does not prove capability presence
  + feature absence does not prove interface absence

& [ReferencePolicy] is Cantor's structural decision over one reference target before library construction
& [DenyRetriever] is a zero-capability sentinel installed at the unavoidable library seam
& [RetrieverInvocationFault] means preflight and construction assumptions disagreed
  + it is internal fault evidence and never accepted resolution

& [ProbeDenyRetriever] is private test-local evidence for dependency admission
& [CantorDenyRetriever] is later production behavior owned by I03D
  + they share a contract shape but never authority lineage

& [MetaSchemaObservation] is a stable report about schema acceptability
& [ValidatorConstructionObservation] is a stable report about public builder construction
  + the identities are separate
  + their engine work is not asserted to be disjoint because public construction repeats validation

& [FormatAnnotationMode] means format keywords are not assertion failures
  + validate formats is false
  + unknown formats are ignored
  + no custom format registry exists

& [RevisedNoResolution] is feature exclusion plus structural preflight plus explicit denial sentinel plus invocation-fault accounting
& [RefinedDisposition] is exact_inactive_dependency_probe_revision_candidate
